abstract:
In this paper, we investigate the $(p_{1}(x), p_{2}(x))$-Laplace operator, the properties of the corresponding integral functional and weak solutions to the related differential equations. We show that the integral functional admits a derivative of type $(S_+)$ which induces a homeomorphism between duality space pairs. As applications of the above results, we gave some existence results of the $(p_{1}(x), p_{2}(x))$-Laplace equation -	ext{div}(|
abla u|^{p_{1}(x)-2}
abla u)-	ext{div}(|
abla u|^{p_{2}(x)-2}
abla u)=f(x,u) in a bounded smooth domain $Ω\subset\mathbb{R}^{N}$ with Dirichlet boundary condition.
